      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "Few studies have investigated the use of dexmedetomidine in obstetric anaesthesia."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To evaluate the effect of dexmedetomidine combined with sufentanil for patient-controlled analgesia (PCA) after caesarean section under spinal anaesthesia."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "DESIGN",
          "content": "An interventional, randomised, double-blinded, placebo-controlled clinical study."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "SETTING",
          "content": "Department of Anaesthesiology, Obstetrics and Gynecology Hospital of Fudan University, Shanghai, China."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "PATIENTS",
          "content": "One hundred and twenty parturients (American Society of Anesthesiologists class 1 or 2) scheduled for elective caesarean delivery under spinal anaesthesia randomly allocated into three groups (n\u200a=\u200a40 each)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "INTERVENTIONS",
          "content": "Group 1: physiological saline bolus after delivery and sufentanil PCA, Group 2: dexmedetomidine bolus (0.5\u200aμg\u200akg) after delivery and sufentanil PCA, Group 3: dexmedetomidine bolus (0.5\u200aμg\u200akg) after delivery and sufentanil with dexmedetomidine PCA (background infusion of 0.045\u200aμg\u200akg\u200ah with a bolus of 0.07\u200aμg\u200akg)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "MAIN OUTCOME MEASURES",
          "content": "The total consumption of sufentanil. Pain scores at rest evaluated with a visual analogue scale (VAS) and Ramsay sedation score (RSS) were recorded at the 4, 8 and 24\u200ah after surgery. The patients' pain threshold (PTh) and pain tolerance threshold (PTTh) were measured before surgery and 1\u200ah after initial study drug administration. Satisfaction scores were collected 24\u200ah after surgery."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "Sufentanil consumption in group 3 was 43.9\u200a±\u200a19.2\u200aμg, significantly lower than in group 1 (54.5\u200a±\u200a23.9\u200aμg) and group 2 (56.3\u200a±\u200a20.6\u200aμg) (P\u200a<\u200a0.05). Compared with group 3, VAS was increased at 4, 8 and 24\u200ah after surgery in groups 1 and 2 (P\u200a<\u200a0.05); there was no difference between groups 1 and 2. PTh and PTTh were significantly increased 1\u200ah after drug administration in groups 2 (1.59\u200a±\u200a0.45, 2.57\u200a±\u200a0.46\u200amA) and 3 (1.74\u200a±\u200a0.37, 2.56\u200a±\u200a0.48\u200amA) compared with group 1 (1.49\u200a±\u200a0.49, 2.42\u200a±\u200a0.62\u200amA) (P\u200a<\u200a0.05)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "The combination of sufentanil and dexmedetomidine for PCA after caesarean section can reduce sufentanil consumption and improve parturients' satisfaction compared with sufentanil PCA alone."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "TRIAL REGISTRATION",
          "content": "ChiCTR-TRC-11001442."
        }
      ]},
